  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA value remains network-concentrated:</strong> the top chains continue to capture the majority of distributed issuance and often set near-term market direction. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/web3/2026/08/22/web3-gaming-network-sandbox-stops-base-and-bnb-chain-bridging-after-exploit\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Web3 gaming network Sandbox stops Base and BNB chain bridging after exploit</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Institutional expansion is likely staged:</strong> large-scale adoption typically lands on proven networks first, then broadens as compliance, interoperability, and liquidity deepen. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-08-21-crypto-is-still-in-winter-price-wise-but-an-institutional-summer-sts-digital-ceo-says-412454\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Crypto is still in \u2018winter\u2019 price-wise but it\u2019s an \u2018institutional summer,\u2019 STS Digital CEO says</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Custody and issuance integrations are moving rankings first:</strong> Chains that win custody and issuance integrations usually pull distributed value share before the broader RWA market total catches up. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/policy/2026/08/21/nomura-backed-laser-digital-wins-japan-s-first-crypto-approval-in-four-years\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nomura-backed Laser Digital wins Japan&#x27;s first crypto approval in four years</a> (CoinDesk).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observation